{
  "summary": "Survey large source files in CipherBox and propose split/refactor plans, with deep dives on the two giants",
  "agentCount": 28,
  "logs": [],
  "result": {
    "assessments": [
      {
        "file": "packages/sdk/src/client.ts",
        "loc": 2643,
        "language": "typescript",
        "summary": "Single large class CipherBoxClient — the stateful public SDK entrypoint consumed by apps/web and apps/desktop. Orchestrates owned-folder CRUD, file upload/download/versioning, recycle-bin ops, share/shared-folder writes, BYO-IPFS pinning mode selection, and event/lifecycle plumbing, holding internal state (folderTree, sharedFolderTree, keyCache, binState) and delegating actual work to stateless sdk-core and sibling op modules (bin/, share/, reencrypt).",
        "responsibilities": [
          {
            "name": "Lifecycle, state access & internal helpers",
            "approxLines": 290,
            "description": "Constructor (defensive key copy, ctx/emitter/tree init, external provider wiring), destroy() key zeroing, hasFolder/getFolder*/registerFolder bridges, @internal getters (getFolderTree/getContext/getConfig/emitEvent), IPNS-name collection helpers (collectSubtreeIpnsNames, collectRemovedItemIpnsNames, collectBinEntryIpnsNames, fireAndForgetUnenroll), reWrapNewItems, getBinContext/getShareContext, withOperation/notifySafely wrapper. Cohesive class glue."
          },
          {
            "name": "Event subscription",
            "approxLines": 12,
            "description": "on/off pass-throughs to SdkEventEmitter."
          },
          {
            "name": "Owned-folder operations",
            "approxLines": 300,
            "description": "loadFolder, ensureFolderLoaded (DFS self-bootstrap from root), requireFolder, createFolder, renameItem, moveItem (with file-metadata re-encryption), deleteItem. Owns folderTree publish + sequence bookkeeping."
          },
          {
            "name": "Owned-file operations & versioning",
            "approxLines": 440,
            "description": "uploadFile, uploadFiles (p-limit batch), replaceFile, restoreFileVersion, deleteFileVersion, maybePublishKeyMigration, downloadFromIpns, downloadFile."
          },
          {
            "name": "Recycle-bin operations",
            "approxLines": 225,
            "description": "loadBin (anti-clobber guard), deleteToBin, restoreFromBin, permanentDelete, emptyBin, purgeExpired. Thin wrappers over bin/ module owning binState + bin:updated emission."
          },
          {
            "name": "Share & shared-folder operations",
            "approxLines": 500,
            "description": "shareFolder, revokeShare, reWrapForRecipients (key-sharing), plus the REQ-3 shared-folder write surface: load/has/get/unload/requireSharedFolder, buildSharedWriteContextFromState, adoptSharedFolderResult, uploadToSharedFolder, createSharedSubfolder, renameInSharedFolder, deleteFromSharedFolder, updateSharedFile, refreshSharedFolder, moveInSharedFolder (key unwrap + zeroing), enumerateSharedSubtree (DFS)."
          },
          {
            "name": "BYO-IPFS pinning mode",
            "approxLines": 85,
            "description": "pinWithMode — cipherbox/external(kubo,pinata,psa)/dual mode dispatch, CID registration, secondary-mirror best-effort. Self-contained policy logic with no folderTree dependency."
          }
        ],
        "splitPlan": [
          {
            "proposedFile": "packages/sdk/src/pinning.ts",
            "moves": "The pinWithMode dispatch logic and external-provider construction (the constructor block choosing Kubo/Pinata/Psa providers) become a stateless module: pinWithMode(provider, pinningConfig, encData, ctx, onProgress) plus a createExternalProvider(pinningConfig) factory. Client keeps a thin private wrapper.",
            "rationale": "Self-contained pinning-mode policy with zero coupling to folderTree/binState/events — purest extraction, mirrors the existing stateless-module pattern (sdk-core providers live in sdk-core already). Independently unit-testable (client-pinning.test.ts already exists and could target the module directly)."
          },
          {
            "proposedFile": "packages/sdk/src/shared-folder.ts",
            "moves": "The ~500 lines of shared-folder surface: requireSharedFolder, buildSharedWriteContextFromState, adoptSharedFolderResult, uploadToSharedFolder, createSharedSubfolder, renameInSharedFolder, deleteFromSharedFolder, updateSharedFile, refreshSharedFolder, moveInSharedFolder, enumerateSharedSubtree — refactored as functions taking (sharedFolderTree, ctx, emitter, args), paralleling how bin/ and share/ already work. Client keeps thin delegating methods to preserve the public API.",
            "rationale": "Largest separable concern. It operates on sharedFolderTree (a distinct map, keyed by shareId) and the existing share/shared-write.ts already holds the stateless logic — these client methods are mostly state-bookkeeping wrappers that belong next to it. Extraction does not change the public method signatures consumers depend on."
          }
        ],
        "verdict": "split-worthwhile",
        "effort": "medium",
        "risk": "medium",
        "impact": "medium",
        "blastRadius": "Public entrypoint of @cipherbox/sdk, re-exported from packages/sdk/src/index.ts as CipherBoxClient (+ BinNotLoadedError). External consumers: apps/web (stores/folder.store.ts, stores/bin.store.ts, hooks/useBin.ts, hooks/useFolderMutations.ts, hooks/shared-folder-projection.ts, lib/sdk-provider.ts, services/share.service.ts) and apps/desktop via the published package. Strong adjacent test coverage: ~22 test files in packages/sdk/src/__tests__/ including client.test.ts, client-extended.test.ts, client-file-ops.test.ts, client-pinning.test.ts, client-move-reencrypt.test.ts, client-shared-write.test.ts, ensure-folder-loaded.test.ts, upload-batch.test.ts, move-in-shared-folder.test.ts. Public surface MUST stay stable (web+desktop consume it) — extraction must be internal-only (delegating wrappers), keeping all method signatures and the index.ts exports unchanged.",
        "notes": "Honest verdict: worthwhile, not strongly recommended. This is a single cohesive class (the stateful orchestration facade), and much of its bulk is irreducible state-bookkeeping glue — extracting every method would just scatter the folderTree mutation logic and hurt readability. The two extractions proposed are the genuinely separable concerns: (1) pinWithMode is pure policy with no shared state — cleanest win; (2) the shared-folder surface operates on a separate map (sharedFolderTree) and parallels the already-extracted share/shared-write.ts, so it reads as a bolt-on rather than core. The constraint that the public surface must stay stable means the split must be internal: move logic to modules taking (tree/ctx/emitter) params and keep the client's methods as one-line delegations (exactly the pattern bin/ and share/ already use). Leave owned-folder + owned-file + bin wrappers in client.ts — splitting those would fragment the folderTree write path that ties them together. Net effect: ~2643 LoC down to roughly 1.9-2.0k, with the two most independent slices testable in isolation. The vitest include is src/**/*.test.ts so new module tests must use .test.ts not .spec.ts."
      },
      {
        "file": "apps/web/src/components/file-browser/SharedFileBrowser.tsx",
        "loc": 946,
        "language": "tsx",
        "summary": "A single React component rendering the \"shared with me\" file browser. It bundles three separable concerns into one function: (1) all the handler/state logic (navigation wiring, 6 dialog states, multi-select, inline rename, inline new-folder, drag-and-drop, an auto-open-editor effect), (2) a ~125-line top-level shared-items list render branch, and (3) a ~370-line folder-view render branch with toolbar, file list, context menu, and 7 dialog instances. It is the shared-content counterpart to the private-vault FileBrowser, which has already been refactored into a thin shell.",
        "responsibilities": [
          {
            "name": "Handler + state logic (callbacks, dialog/selection/rename/folder/drag state, auto-open effect)",
            "approxLines": 375,
            "description": "Lines ~99-443: useState/useRef for 6 dialog states, contextShareId, new-folder input, drag state, move dialog, multi-select Set, batch-move, inline rename; ~20 useCallback handlers (download, details, edit, preview, hide, upload, create folder, rename, delete, drag/drop, select); two pruning/clearing effects; and the writable-file auto-open-editor effect."
          },
          {
            "name": "Top-level shared list render branch",
            "approxLines": 127,
            "description": "Lines ~446-572: the `currentView === 'list'` early return — breadcrumb, loading/error/empty states, the shared-items grid with synthetic-FolderChild context-menu wiring, a read-only ContextMenu, and a DetailsDialog."
          },
          {
            "name": "Folder view render branch",
            "approxLines": 367,
            "description": "Lines ~578-945: breadcrumb nav, write toolbar (upload/mkdir + hidden input), SelectionActionBar, inline new-folder input, loading/error/empty states, file list with ParentDir row and SharedFolderRow mapping incl. drag-move routing, the permission-aware ContextMenu, two SharedMoveDialogs, and 6 preview/editor dialog instances."
          },
          {
            "name": "Module-local pure helpers + constants",
            "approxLines": 25,
            "description": "Lines ~47-70: sortItems() (folders-first sort), DialogState type, and the sharedEmptyArt ASCII constant."
          }
        ],
        "splitPlan": [
          {
            "proposedFile": "apps/web/src/components/file-browser/useSharedFileBrowserActions.ts",
            "moves": "All handler logic and state: the 6 dialog states (migrate to the existing useDialogState hook), contextShareId, new-folder input state, drag state, move/batch-move dialog state, multi-select Set + handleSelect/clearSelection + prune/clear effects, inline rename state, and every useCallback handler (download/details/edit/preview/hide/upload/createFolder/rename/delete/drag-drop), plus the auto-open-editor useEffect. Returns a typed object consumed by the shell, exactly mirroring useFileBrowserActions.ts.",
            "rationale": "The codebase already established this exact pattern for the private vault (FileBrowser.tsx delegates to useFileBrowserActions.ts). Applying it here removes ~375 lines of imperative logic from the component, makes the handlers unit-testable in isolation, and aligns the shared browser with its sibling's architecture."
          },
          {
            "proposedFile": "apps/web/src/components/file-browser/SharedListView.tsx",
            "moves": "The entire `currentView === 'list'` render branch (breadcrumb, states, shared-items grid with the synthetic-FolderChild builder, read-only ContextMenu, DetailsDialog). Takes sharedItems, navigation callbacks, and contextMenu/dialog props.",
            "rationale": "The list view and folder view are visually and structurally disjoint (different columns: SHARED BY vs SIZE/MODIFIED, different actions). Extracting it makes each render path independently readable and isolates the synthetic-FolderChild construction that currently clutters the parent."
          },
          {
            "proposedFile": "apps/web/src/components/file-browser/sharedBrowser.helpers.ts",
            "moves": "sortItems() and the sharedEmptyArt constant (and optionally the synthetic FolderChild builder used in the list view).",
            "rationale": "Small pure helpers shared by both views belong in a sibling module so they can be reused by the extracted list view and unit-tested without rendering."
          }
        ],
        "verdict": "split-worthwhile",
        "effort": "medium",
        "risk": "medium",
        "impact": "high",
        "blastRadius": "Importers are only two: re-exported from apps/web/src/components/file-browser/index.ts and consumed by apps/web/src/routes/SharedPage.tsx (used as <SharedFileBrowser /> with no props). The public component signature stays unchanged, so both importers are unaffected — extractions are internal. NO test coverage exists: no SharedFileBrowser test/spec file and no __tests__ dir in file-browser/. This raises regression risk because the refactor is unguarded; recommend adding tests for the extracted hook first (and note apps/web vitest only runs *.test.ts, not *.spec.ts).",
        "notes": "Split is worthwhile rather than strongly-recommended only because the file is internally well-organized and single-purpose; the strongest justification is convergence with the existing FileBrowser/useFileBrowserActions pattern (the dedicated useDialogState hook already exists and is unused here). The riskiest extraction is the hook: several handlers depend on currentView/contextShareId/sharedItems from useSharedNavigation and on each other (e.g. handleCreateFolderSubmit feeds handleCreateFolderKeyDown), and the auto-open-editor effect has subtle deps — preserve the dependency arrays exactly. The >1 multi-select gating (lines 149-154) and drag-move routing-by-dragged-not-selected logic (lines 756-777) carry load-bearing comments; keep them intact. Add tests before/with the refactor since there is currently none."
      },
      {
        "file": "apps/desktop/src/auth.ts",
        "loc": 800,
        "language": "typescript",
        "summary": "Desktop webview auth module. Authenticates via CipherBox identity provider (Google OAuth, Email OTP, SIWE wallet), runs Web3Auth MPC Core Kit loginWithJWT to derive the TSS key, handles MFA (recovery-phrase and device-approval bulletin-board flows), and hands the exported private key + JWT to the Rust backend over Tauri IPC. Also owns a self-contained Google OAuth popup/localhost-callback orchestrator.",
        "responsibilities": [
          {
            "name": "Core Kit lifecycle & config",
            "approxLines": 75,
            "description": "Module imports, env/config constants (API_BASE, client IDs, NETWORK_MAP), the coreKit singleton, LoginResult type, initCoreKit, getCoreKitStatus."
          },
          {
            "name": "Identity login flows + Core Kit handoff",
            "approxLines": 260,
            "description": "loginWithGoogle, requestEmailOtp, loginWithEmailOtp, loginWithWallet (SIWE), shared loginWithCoreKit (incl. REQUIRED_SHARE temp-token), completeAuthHandoff, restoreSession, logout."
          },
          {
            "name": "MFA recovery & device approval",
            "approxLines": 225,
            "description": "inputRecoveryPhrase, requestDeviceApproval, pollApprovalStatus, cancelApprovalRequest, approveDevice — ephemeral keypair, ECIES wrap/unwrap, createFactor/setDeviceFactor, bulletin-board fetch calls. Owns ephemeralPrivateKey module state."
          },
          {
            "name": "Device identity helpers",
            "approxLines": 35,
            "description": "getDesktopDeviceId (localStorage persisted SHA-256 id), getDeviceName (UA sniff), getAccessToken accessor."
          },
          {
            "name": "Google OAuth popup orchestration",
            "approxLines": 95,
            "description": "getGoogleCredential — start_oauth_server IPC, listen for port-scoped Tauri callback event, state/nonce validation, popup open, 2-min timeout, cleanup."
          }
        ],
        "splitPlan": [
          {
            "proposedFile": "apps/desktop/src/auth/corekit.ts",
            "moves": "coreKit singleton, NETWORK_MAP/config consts, initCoreKit, getCoreKitStatus, loginWithCoreKit, completeAuthHandoff, restoreSession, logout, LoginResult type, and the lastCipherboxJwt/temporaryAccessToken module state plus small accessors.",
            "rationale": "Centralizes the Core Kit singleton and the shared module-mutable auth state so the other modules import accessors instead of re-declaring globals. This is the coupling hub and must be extracted first."
          },
          {
            "proposedFile": "apps/desktop/src/auth/login.ts",
            "moves": "loginWithGoogle, requestEmailOtp, loginWithEmailOtp, loginWithWallet (SIWE message build + verify). Imports loginWithCoreKit from corekit.ts and getGoogleCredential from oauth.ts.",
            "rationale": "The four identity providers are a cohesive group of public entry points; isolating them keeps provider-specific fetch/SIWE logic out of the Core Kit core."
          },
          {
            "proposedFile": "apps/desktop/src/auth/mfa.ts",
            "moves": "inputRecoveryPhrase, requestDeviceApproval, pollApprovalStatus, cancelApprovalRequest, approveDevice, plus ephemeralPrivateKey state and createDeviceFactor (extract the duplicated createFactor/setDeviceFactor/commitChanges block shared by recovery + approval).",
            "rationale": "Largest separable concern; depends only on Core Kit accessors + device helpers + crypto. The duplicated device-factor block is begging to be a single helper."
          },
          {
            "proposedFile": "apps/desktop/src/auth/device.ts",
            "moves": "getDesktopDeviceId, getDeviceName, getAccessToken.",
            "rationale": "Tiny shared utilities consumed by both mfa.ts and corekit.ts; keeps them dependency-free and trivially testable."
          },
          {
            "proposedFile": "apps/desktop/src/auth/oauth.ts",
            "moves": "getGoogleCredential and its Tauri IPC/event plumbing.",
            "rationale": "Self-contained popup+callback orchestrator with its own lifecycle/cleanup; the only Google-OAuth Tauri-event code in the app and naturally standalone."
          },
          {
            "proposedFile": "apps/desktop/src/auth/index.ts",
            "moves": "Re-export the public surface currently imported by main.ts so the import path stays './auth'.",
            "rationale": "Preserves the single importer's path and keeps the change a pure internal reshuffle with no caller edits."
          }
        ],
        "verdict": "split-worthwhile",
        "effort": "medium",
        "risk": "medium",
        "impact": "medium",
        "blastRadius": "Single importer: apps/desktop/src/main.ts (named imports ending at the `} from './auth'` block). No test files exist for this module and the desktop app has no vitest config, so there is zero adjacent test coverage — meaning a refactor has no safety net and must be verified manually (login + MFA flows). Not part of the published @cipherbox/sdk surface, so no cross-package contract impact. Keeping a barrel at apps/desktop/src/auth/index.ts means main.ts needs no changes.",
        "notes": "Verdict is split-worthwhile, not strongly recommended: the file is large but genuinely multi-concern (5 distinct responsibilities, only one importer). The main risk is the shared module-level mutable state — coreKit, lastCipherboxJwt, temporaryAccessToken, ephemeralPrivateKey — which is read/written across the login, MFA, and handoff functions. A naive file split that scatters these globals would break the auth state machine; the corekit.ts module must own that state and expose accessors/mutators, which is the bulk of the effort and risk. Convert the convert-to-barrel safely by keeping './auth' path. Secondary cleanup: the createFactor/setDeviceFactor/commitChanges block is duplicated verbatim in inputRecoveryPhrase and pollApprovalStatus (and platform is hardcoded 'macos' in both) — fold into one createDeviceFactor helper during the move. Given zero test coverage, write at least light unit tests for device.ts helpers and the SIWE message builder as part of the split, and manually exercise Google/Email/Wallet + recovery-phrase + device-approval before merging."
      },
      {
        "file": "apps/web/src/components/file-browser/ShareDialog.tsx",
        "loc": 786,
        "language": "tsx",
        "summary": "A modal dialog for sharing files/folders with another user by public key. It mixes three concerns: a large body of client-side crypto orchestration (unwrapping owner keys, re-wrapping folder/file/IPNS keys for a recipient, traversing folder descendants), the share-management data layer (fetching/paginating sent shares, create/revoke/upgrade/downgrade permission via API + Zustand stores), and a ~280-line \"direct share\" tab UI (input, permission toggle, recipients list with inline confirm controls). The invite-link tab is already extracted to a sibling InviteLinkTab.tsx.",
        "responsibilities": [
          {
            "name": "Pubkey validation/formatting helpers",
            "approxLines": 20,
            "description": "isValidPublicKey and truncateKey pure helpers (lines 45-63), reusable display/validation logic with no React deps."
          },
          {
            "name": "Share creation crypto orchestration (handleShare)",
            "approxLines": 216,
            "description": "Lines 174-390: validation, recipient lookup, folder vs file branching, unwrap/wrap folder key + IPNS key, collectChildKeys traversal, encrypted itemName, API create call, store update. The crypto-heavy core."
          },
          {
            "name": "Permission/revoke mutation logic",
            "approxLines": 100,
            "description": "handleRevoke, handleUpgrade, handleDowngradeConfirm (lines 392-489): unwrap/re-wrap IPNS key for upgrade, API calls via share.service, local + store state sync."
          },
          {
            "name": "Sent-shares fetch + pagination + state reset",
            "approxLines": 68,
            "description": "useEffect (lines 104-172) paginating sharesControllerGetSentShares filtered by ipnsName, plus full state reset on close."
          },
          {
            "name": "Component state declarations",
            "approxLines": 16,
            "description": "Lines 84-102: ~17 useState plus refs spanning all three concerns."
          },
          {
            "name": "Direct-share tab JSX",
            "approxLines": 235,
            "description": "Lines 503-771: tab bar, input/permission UI, recipients list with upgrade/downgrade/revoke inline-confirm buttons. Large presentational block."
          }
        ],
        "splitPlan": [
          {
            "proposedFile": "apps/web/src/components/file-browser/share/share-pubkey.ts",
            "moves": "isValidPublicKey and truncateKey pure helpers",
            "rationale": "Pure, framework-free, trivially unit-testable; reused by display (truncateKey appears 5+ times in JSX) and validation. Mirrors the existing extraction of key-wrapping.ts out of this same file."
          },
          {
            "proposedFile": "apps/web/src/components/file-browser/share/useDirectShare.ts",
            "moves": "All share state (useState/refs), the sent-shares fetch+pagination useEffect, handleShare crypto orchestration, handleRevoke/handleUpgrade/handleDowngradeConfirm, handleKeyDown. Returns state + handlers.",
            "rationale": "Concentrates the heavy crypto + API + store logic (~480 lines) into a testable hook, leaving ShareDialog as a thin presentational shell. Follows the local useFileBrowserActions.ts hook convention."
          },
          {
            "proposedFile": "apps/web/src/components/file-browser/share/RecipientsList.tsx",
            "moves": "The recipients-section JSX (lines 648-769): per-recipient row with upgrade/downgrade/revoke inline-confirm buttons, driven by props from the hook.",
            "rationale": "~120 lines of self-contained list-item rendering with intricate conditional confirm states; isolating it shrinks the dialog and makes the confirm-state logic easier to follow. Matches sibling pattern (SharedFolderRow, SharedListRow, BinListItem)."
          }
        ],
        "verdict": "split-worthwhile",
        "effort": "medium",
        "risk": "medium",
        "impact": "high",
        "blastRadius": "Public surface is just the ShareDialog component, imported in exactly one place: apps/web/src/components/file-browser/FileBrowser.tsx (line 22, rendered at line 294). useFileBrowserActions.ts owns the open/close wiring but does not import the component. No adjacent test file exists for ShareDialog and there is no __tests__ dir in file-browser, so refactors are validated only by typecheck/build and manual/Puppeteer flows — raising regression risk for the crypto path (folder traversal, IPNS write-share key wrapping). Splitting into a share/ subfolder keeps the single import stable (only the export path of ShareDialog matters) while creating natural unit-test seams (share-pubkey.ts, useDirectShare.ts).",
        "notes": "The file is not one cohesive unit — crypto orchestration, the share data/mutation layer, and tab UI are cleanly separable, and the team already established this exact extraction pattern (key-wrapping.ts header reads \"Extracted from ShareDialog\", InviteLinkTab.tsx is a sibling tab). Highest value is moving handleShare and the permission mutations into useDirectShare.ts: that logic is security-sensitive (key unwrapping, fill(0) zeroization, write-share IPNS key handling) and currently has zero test coverage. Caution during the split: preserve the exact try/finally key.fill(0) zeroization blocks and the effectivePermission downgrade-when-no-IPNS-key logic — these are security invariants per CLAUDE.md. Suggest extracting helpers first (low risk), then the hook, verifying with pnpm typecheck/build between steps since there is no test safety net. Note a latent pre-existing concern unrelated to the split: handleShare reads vaultKeypair.privateKey but never zeroizes recipientPubKeyBytes/keypair refs and double-wraps the file IPNS key (lines 313 and 317 wrap the same ipnsPrivKey twice) — flag, do not fix, during refactor."
      },
      {
        "file": "apps/web/src/hooks/useAuth.ts",
        "loc": 732,
        "language": "typescript",
        "summary": "The web app's central authentication hook. It wires Web3Auth Core Kit login (Google/Email/Wallet), the REQUIRED_SHARE MFA flow, backend JWT auth, full vault initialization/loading (IPNS key blob + folder metadata + SDK client bootstrap + BYO pinning config + device registry + bin), session restoration on reload, and logout. A large amount of non-React orchestration logic is inlined inside React callbacks.",
        "responsibilities": [
          {
            "name": "Vault init/load orchestration",
            "approxLines": 230,
            "description": "initializeOrLoadVault: module-level dedup promise, getVault 404 detection, new-user vault creation (key blob v2 publish, folder metadata publish, vault register), existing-vault key decryption via IPNS, SDK client construction with share callbacks, and fire-and-forget device-registry + bin bootstrap. Pure async orchestration that touches stores directly, not React state."
          },
          {
            "name": "BYO pinning config loader",
            "approxLines": 50,
            "description": "Nested loadByoConfig: derive BYO IPNS keypair, resolve+fetch+decrypt+validate ByoIpfsConfig with a 10s timeout race. Self-contained, no React dependency."
          },
          {
            "name": "Backend auth completion",
            "approxLines": 40,
            "description": "completeBackendAuth: export Core Kit publicKey, call authApi.login, store token, run vault init, mark authenticated, set Faro user."
          },
          {
            "name": "Login flows (Google/Email/Wallet)",
            "approxLines": 140,
            "description": "Three near-identical callbacks each handling normal vs required_share branch, temp-token acquisition, and error/loading toggles. Significant duplication of the required_share temp-login block."
          },
          {
            "name": "REQUIRED_SHARE completion",
            "approxLines": 30,
            "description": "completeRequiredShare: read pending JWT/method from store, finish backend auth, sync Core Kit status, navigate."
          },
          {
            "name": "Logout",
            "approxLines": 35,
            "description": "Backend logout, Core Kit logout, clear all stores, clear Faro, navigate."
          },
          {
            "name": "Session restoration effect + hook state/wiring",
            "approxLines": 120,
            "description": "isLoading derivation, refs to stabilize the restore effect, the restoreSession useEffect (refresh cookie -> vault load -> authenticate), store selectors, and the returned API surface. This is the genuinely React-bound glue."
          }
        ],
        "splitPlan": [
          {
            "proposedFile": "apps/web/src/services/vault-init.service.ts",
            "moves": "Extract initializeOrLoadVault as a plain async service function (e.g. initializeOrLoadVault({ userKeypair }) or taking getVaultKeypair). Move the module-level vaultInitPromise dedup, new-user creation (key blob v2 + folder metadata publish + vault register), existing-vault decrypt path, SDK client construction with shareCallbacks, and the fire-and-forget device-registry + bin bootstrap blocks. It already operates almost entirely on Zustand getState()/setState and SDK/api modules, so it needs no React.",
            "rationale": "This is ~280 LoC of the file and is pure orchestration with zero React state usage (only getVaultKeypair/setVaultKeypair/setVaultKeys, all passable). Moving it to services/ matches the existing convention (ipns.service, vault-settings.service, share.service) and makes the largest, most testable concern independently unit-testable. Biggest single win."
          },
          {
            "proposedFile": "apps/web/src/services/byo-config.service.ts",
            "moves": "Extract the nested loadByoConfig (derive BYO IPNS keypair, resolve/fetch/decrypt/validate ByoIpfsConfig, 10s timeout race) into a standalone exported loadByoPinningConfig(userPrivateKey).",
            "rationale": "Fully self-contained, no React, parallels loadVaultSettings in vault-settings.service. Removing the nested function declutters initializeOrLoadVault and gives a focused, testable unit. Can be done together with the vault-init extraction."
          },
          {
            "proposedFile": "apps/web/src/services/auth-flow.service.ts (optional)",
            "moves": "Optionally factor the repeated required_share temp-login block (authApi.login with `pending-core-kit-${userId}` placeholder + setAccessToken) shared by loginWithGoogle/Email/Wallet into a helper acquireTempBackendToken(jwt, userId).",
            "rationale": "The three login callbacks duplicate the temp-token acquisition verbatim. A small helper removes ~30 LoC of duplication. Low priority vs the vault extraction; keep the login callbacks themselves in the hook since they own React loading/error state."
          }
        ],
        "verdict": "split-worthwhile",
        "effort": "medium",
