  "clientDeepDive": "The consumers use `getContext()` and `ensureFolderLoaded()` publicly (despite `@internal` tags), plus the documented public methods. This confirms the facade must preserve the full surface including the `@internal`-tagged accessors. I have enough to produce the plan.\n\n# Refactor Plan: Decompose `packages/sdk/src/client.ts` (2643 LoC)\n\n## 1. Executive summary\n\n`CipherBoxClient` is a single 2643-line class that mixes eight responsibilities over a small set of shared private fields (`folderTree`, `sharedFolderTree`, `binState`, `keyCache`, `ctx`, `config`, `emitter`, `externalProvider`, internal key copies). The class is consumed by `apps/web` and `apps/desktop` and its surface — including several `@internal`-tagged accessors that are actually called externally — **must not break**.\n\nRecommended approach: **composition behind a thin facade**. Extract cohesive operation groups into stateless-ish modules that receive a shared `ClientCore` handle (the bag of shared state + helpers), then keep `CipherBoxClient` as a thin delegating facade that preserves every current public method signature verbatim. This matches the already-established `bin/` and `share/` pattern (functions + an explicit `*OperationContext`), so it is the lowest-novelty, lowest-risk option.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Public/exported surface inventory, grouped by responsibility\n\nLine ranges are approximate against the current file.\n\n### Module-level exports (must remain stable)\n- `class BinNotLoadedError` (L46–51) — re-exported from `index.ts`.\n- `class CipherBoxClient` (L53–2643).\n\n### A. Construction / lifecycle (L77–264)\n- `constructor` (L77–124) — builds `ctx`, defensive key copies, `externalProvider`, the three state containers.\n- `destroy()` (L249–264).\n\n### B. Event subscription (L126–136)\n- `on(handler)`, `off(handler)`.\n\n### C. Internal-state accessors (public surface — externally called) (L266–355)\n- `hasFolder` (L272), `getFolderSequenceNumber` (L280), `getFolderIpnsPrivateKey` (L291), `registerFolder` (L313).\n- `getFolderTree` (L338), `getContext` (L343), `getConfig` (L348), `emitEvent` (L353). Tagged `@internal` but `getContext()` and `ensureFolderLoaded()` are called from `apps/web` (`folder-helpers.ts`, `useFileBrowserActions.ts`, `useFolderNavigation.ts`). **Treat as public.**\n\n### D. Folder operations (L357–860)\n- `loadFolder` (L370), `ensureFolderLoaded` (L444, externally called), `requireFolder` (private, L527), `createFolder` (L544), `renameItem` (L645), `moveItem` (L702, uses `reencryptFileMetadataForFolderChange`), `deleteItem` (L816).\n\n### E. File upload/download + version history (L862–1706)\n- `uploadFile` (L877), `uploadFiles` (L1057), `replaceFile` (L1335), `restoreFileVersion` (L1444), `deleteFileVersion` (L1526), `maybePublishKeyMigration` (private, L1601), `downloadFromIpns` (L1646), `downloadFile` (L1684).\n\n### F. Bin / trash (L1708–1933)\n- `loadBin` (L1716), `deleteToBin` (L1761), `restoreFromBin` (L1810), `permanentDelete` (L1848), `emptyBin` (L1874), `purgeExpired` (L1904). All delegate to `binOps` via `getBinContext()`.\n\n### G. Share (owned-folder sharing) (L1935–1997)\n- `shareFolder` (L1944), `revokeShare` (L1966), `reWrapForRecipients` (L1982). Delegate to `shareOps` via `getShareContext()`.\n\n### H. Shared-folder (write-share recipient) ops (L1999–2501)\n- State: `loadSharedFolder` (L2017), `hasSharedFolder` (L2024), `getSharedFolderState` (L2032), `unloadSharedFolder` (L2037).\n- Private helpers: `requireSharedFolder` (L2045), `buildSharedWriteContextFromState` (L2056), `adoptSharedFolderResult` (L2078).\n- Writes: `uploadToSharedFolder` (L2110), `createSharedSubfolder` (L2127), `renameInSharedFolder` (L2141), `deleteFromSharedFolder` (L2158), `updateSharedFile` (L2183), `refreshSharedFolder` (L2239), `moveInSharedFolder` (L2292), `enumerateSharedSubtree` (L2409).\n\n### I. Pinning / IPFS transport (L2503–2586)\n- `pinWithMode` (private, L2517) — also `externalProvider` init in the constructor.\n\n### J. Cross-cutting private infrastructure\n- IPNS sequence/unenroll + subtree walks: `reWrapNewItems` (L149), `fireAndForgetUnenroll` (L183), `collectRemovedItemIpnsNames` (L204), `collectBinEntryIpnsNames` (L214), `collectSubtreeIpnsNames` (L230).\n- Context builders: `getBinContext` (L2591), `getShareContext` (L2602).\n- Operation wrapper: `withOperation` (L2618), `notifySafely` (L2636).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Existing conventions to follow\n\n- `bin/index.ts` and `share/index.ts` are **stateless function modules** that take an explicit `*OperationContext` (the “replaces Zustand store access” pattern). The client builds these contexts in `getBinContext()` / `getShareContext()` and passes its `folderTree`/`binState` as parameters.\n- `share/context.ts` is a pure builder (`buildSharedWriteContext`) — a good template for any new context builders.\n- State containers live under `state/` (`FolderTree`, `SharedFolderTree`, `KeyCache`).\n- `index.ts` re-exports the class, error, types, events, and the shared-write stateless functions. The barrel is the contract; **do not change its export list**.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Shared private state + how to thread it\n\nThese are the fields every group touches and the reason a naive split is hard:\n\n| State | Read by | Mutated by |\n|---|---|---|\n| `folderTree` | folder, file, bin, sequence accessors, `ensureFolderLoaded` | folder, file, bin |\n| `sharedFolderTree` | shared-folder group | shared-folder group |\n| `binState` | bin group | bin group |\n| `ctx` | every group | constructor only |\n| `config` (keys, callbacks, pinningConfig) | every group | constructor only |\n| `emitter` | every group | constructor / `destroy` |\n| `externalProvider` | file + pinning | constructor |\n| internal key copies | folder bootstrap, download, shared move | `destroy` (zeroing) |\n| `withOperation` | every public async method | — |\n\n### Threading strategy: a `ClientCore` handle (single shared dependency object)\n\nIntroduce one internal object that bundles the shared state and the two cross-cutting helpers (`withOperation`, `emit`). Each extracted module is a class that takes `ClientCore` in its constructor and holds a reference — **not copies** — so there is one source of truth for `folderTree`/`binState`/`sharedFolderTree`.\n\n```ts\n// state/client-core.ts  (NOT exported from index.ts)\nexport interface ClientCore {\n  readonly ctx: SdkContext;\n  readonly config: CipherBoxClientConfig;\n  readonly emitter: SdkEventEmitter;\n  readonly folderTree: FolderTree;\n  readonly sharedFolderTree: SharedFolderTree;\n  readonly keyCache: KeyCache;\n  readonly externalProvider: PinningProvider | null;\n  readonly internalVaultKeypair: { publicKey: Uint8Array; privateKey: Uint8Array };\n  readonly internalRootFolderKey: Uint8Array;\n  readonly internalRootIpnsKeypair: { publicKey: Uint8Array; privateKey: Uint8Array } | null;\n  // binState must be mutable + shared → expose via getter/setter, not a field copy\n  getBinState(): BinState | null;\n  setBinState(s: BinState | null): void;\n  // cross-cutting\n  withOperation<T>(name: string, fn: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T>;\n  emit(e: SdkEvent): void;\n}\n```\n\n`binState` is the one piece of state reassigned (not just mutated) by the owning module, so it must live behind `getBinState()/setBinState()` on `ClientCore` (or stay on the facade with the bin module mutating via accessor) rather than being copied into the bin module — otherwise the facade and module would desync.\n\n`folderTree`, `sharedFolderTree`, `binState` mutation is **always** the in-place pattern already used (`folder.children = ...; this.folderTree.set(...)`), so sharing the reference preserves semantics exactly.\n\nThe cross-cutting IPNS helpers (`fireAndForgetUnenroll`, `collect*IpnsNames`, `reWrapNewItems`) read `folderTree`/`config`/`ctx`/`emitter` — move them into an `ipns-maintenance` module that also takes `ClientCore`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Target file tree\n\n```\npackages/sdk/src/\n  client.ts                     # THIN FACADE: constructor builds ClientCore + sub-modules,\n                                #   every public method delegates one-liner. (~350 LoC)\n  state/\n    client-core.ts             # ClientCore interface + concrete impl bundling shared state\n    folder-tree.ts             # (unchanged)\n    shared-folder-tree.ts      # (unchanged)\n    key-cache.ts               # (unchanged)\n  ops/\n    folder-ops.ts              # FolderOps: loadFolder, ensureFolderLoaded, requireFolder,\n                               #   createFolder, renameItem, moveItem, deleteItem,\n                               #   register/has/getSeq/getIpnsKey accessors\n    file-ops.ts                # FileOps: uploadFile, uploadFiles, downloadFile,\n                               #   downloadFromIpns, pinFn builder\n    version-ops.ts            # VersionOps: replaceFile, restoreFileVersion,\n                               #   deleteFileVersion, maybePublishKeyMigration\n    shared-folder-ops.ts      # SharedFolderOps: all of group H\n    ipns-maintenance.ts       # reWrapNewItems, fireAndForgetUnenroll, collect* walks\n    pinning.ts                # pinWithMode + externalProvider factory\n  bin/                         # (unchanged — already a module; facade keeps delegating)\n  share/                       # (unchanged)\n  reencrypt.ts                 # (unchanged)\n  events.ts  types.ts  error.ts  index.ts   # unchanged\n```\n\nMethod → file map:\n\n| File | Methods moved |\n|---|---|\n| `ops/folder-ops.ts` | `loadFolder`, `ensureFolderLoaded`, `requireFolder`, `createFolder`, `renameItem`, `moveItem`, `deleteItem`, `hasFolder`, `getFolderSequenceNumber`, `getFolderIpnsPrivateKey`, `registerFolder` |\n| `ops/file-ops.ts` | `uploadFile`, `uploadFiles`, `downloadFile`, `downloadFromIpns` |\n| `ops/version-ops.ts` | `replaceFile`, `restoreFileVersion`, `deleteFileVersion`, `maybePublishKeyMigration` |\n| `ops/shared-folder-ops.ts` | all group-H methods + `requireSharedFolder`, `buildSharedWriteContextFromState`, `adoptSharedFolderResult` |\n| `ops/ipns-maintenance.ts` | `reWrapNewItems`, `fireAndForgetUnenroll`, `collectRemovedItemIpnsNames`, `collectBinEntryIpnsNames`, `collectSubtreeIpnsNames` |\n| `ops/pinning.ts` | `pinWithMode`, externalProvider construction |\n| `state/client-core.ts` | `withOperation`, `notifySafely`, `getBinContext`, `getShareContext`, the shared fields, `emit` |\n| `client.ts` (stays) | constructor, `destroy`, `on`/`off`, `getContext`/`getConfig`/`getFolderTree`/`emitEvent`, all bin delegations, all share delegations, and thin delegators to every Ops class |\n\n`requireFolder` is the single self-heal chokepoint and is used by folder, file, and version ops — put it on `FolderOps` and let `FileOps`/`VersionOps` hold a `FolderOps` reference (or expose `requireFolder` on `ClientCore`). Recommended: expose `requireFolder` and `ensureFolderLoaded` on `ClientCore` since they’re shared infrastructure, keeping the `Ops` classes acyclic.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Preservation strategy: thin facade + composition (chosen)\n\n**Choice: composition behind a thin delegating facade.** Justification vs. alternatives:\n\n- **Mixins** (`applyMixins(CipherBoxClient, [FolderMixin, ...])`): TypeScript mixins lose strong typing on `private` shared state, force all groups to share one `this`, and make the “one shared-state object” explicit threading impossible to enforce. They also obscure which group owns what — the opposite of the goal. Reject.\n- **Re-export sub-clients** (make web call `client.folders.createFolder`): breaks the public API. Reject.\n- **Composition + facade**: the facade keeps the exact method names/signatures; internally it instantiates `FolderOps`, `FileOps`, etc., each given `ClientCore`. Every public method becomes a one-line delegate. This:\n  - guarantees zero public-API drift (signatures copied verbatim, `index.ts` untouched),\n  - mirrors the existing `bin/`/`share/` context-passing convention,\n  - keeps the `@internal`-but-externally-used accessors (`getContext`, `ensureFolderLoaded`, `getFolderTree`, etc.) on the facade unchanged.\n\nFacade shape:\n\n```ts\nexport class CipherBoxClient {\n  private core: ClientCoreImpl;\n  private folders: FolderOps;\n  private files: FileOps;\n  private versions: VersionOps;\n  private shared: SharedFolderOps;\n\n  constructor(config) { /* build core + ops; binState/share delegations stay inline */ }\n\n  async createFolder(p, n) { return this.folders.createFolder(p, n); }\n  async uploadFile(...a)   { return this.files.uploadFile(...a); }\n  async replaceFile(...a)  { return this.versions.replaceFile(...a); }\n  ensureFolderLoaded(n)    { return this.core.ensureFolderLoaded(n); }\n  getContext()             { return this.core.ctx; }\n  // ...bin + share keep current inline delegation to binOps/shareOps...\n}\n```\n\nKeep `withOperation` wrapping **inside** the Ops methods (each method already opens with `return this.withOperation(...)`), so the facade delegate is a bare call — no double-wrapping.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Phased, independently-shippable extraction sequence\n\nEach phase: compile + lint clean, full `pnpm --filter @cipherbox/sdk test` green, `pnpm api:generate` not needed (no API change). Ship per phase. Guarding tests named per phase below (all in `packages/sdk/src/__tests__`).\n\n**Phase 0 — Introduce `ClientCore` (no method moves).** Create `state/client-core.ts`, move the shared fields + `withOperation`/`notifySafely`/`getBinContext`/`getShareContext`/`requireFolder`/`ensureFolderLoaded` onto it, have the class hold a `core` and forward. Pure mechanical; everything else still lives in the class.\n- Guards: `client.test.ts`, `context.test.ts`, `ensure-folder-loaded.test.ts`, `client-load-reconcile.test.ts`.\n\n**Phase 1 — Extract `ops/pinning.ts`.** Lowest coupling (only `config`, `ctx`, `externalProvider`, `sdkCore`). Move `pinWithMode` + provider factory.\n- Guards: `client-pinning.test.ts`.\n\n**Phase 2 — Extract `ops/ipns-maintenance.ts`.** The `collect*`/`fireAndForgetUnenroll`/`reWrapNewItems` helpers. Used by folder/file/bin; route calls through `core` or a shared `IpnsMaintenance` instance.\n- Guards: `client.test.ts`, `bin.test.ts` (unenroll paths), `share.test.ts` (re-wrap).\n\n**Phase 3 — Extract `ops/folder-ops.ts`.** `loadFolder`, `createFolder`, `renameItem`, `moveItem`, `deleteItem`, the four sync accessors. `requireFolder`/`ensureFolderLoaded` already on `core` from Phase 0. **Highest folderTree-desync risk — see §8.**\n- Guards: `client.test.ts`, `client-move-reencrypt.test.ts`, `client-load-reconcile.test.ts`, `ensure-folder-loaded.test.ts`, `client-extended.test.ts`.\n\n**Phase 4 — Extract `ops/file-ops.ts`.** `uploadFile`, `uploadFiles`, `downloadFile`, `downloadFromIpns`.\n- Guards: `client-file-ops.test.ts`, `client-upload-concurrency.test.ts`, `upload-batch.test.ts`, `client-pinning.test.ts`.\n\n**Phase 5 — Extract `ops/version-ops.ts`.** `replaceFile`, `restoreFileVersion`, `deleteFileVersion`, `maybePublishKeyMigration`.\n- Guards: `client-file-ops.test.ts`, `client-load-reconcile.test.ts` (sequence-as-clock), `client-extended.test.ts`.\n\n**Phase 6 — Extract `ops/shared-folder-ops.ts`.** All group H. Largest single group; do last because it’s self-contained (operates on `sharedFolderTree`, not `folderTree`).\n- Guards: `client-shared-write.test.ts`, `shared-write.test.ts`, `move-in-shared-folder.test.ts`, `enumerate-shared-subtree.test.ts`, `shared-folder-tree.test.ts`.\n\n**Phase 7 — Facade cleanup.** Collapse remaining inline bin/share delegations to one-liners; verify `client.ts` is ~350 LoC of pure delegation. Run `integration.test.ts` against a local stack (per memory: `docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml up -d` + `pnpm --filter @cipherbox/api dev`) since it is skipped in CI.\n- Guards: full suite + `integration.test.ts` locally; `bin.test.ts`, `share.test.ts`, `events.test.ts`, `error.test.ts`.\n\nNote (from memory): apps/web vitest `include` is `*.test.ts` only — these `.test.ts` names are correct and will actually run.\n\n---\n\n## 8. The two explicit risks\n\n### folderTree desync (Zustand ↔ SDK `folderTree`, #489 sequence-as-clock)\nFolder state lives in **both** the web Zustand `useFolderStore` and the SDK `folderTree`; direct sdk-core publishes that bypass `folderTree` cause stale-sequence 409s and resurrect deleted files. The current code defends this with the **sequence-as-clock invariant** (`loadFolder` L386–396, `refreshSharedFolder` L2254, `adoptSharedFolderResult` re-read-live L2085) and the **adopt-`publishedChildren` (CR-01)** write-back after every publish.\n\nMitigation across the refactor:\n- **Single source of truth:** `ClientCore.folderTree` is shared by reference — never copied into an Ops module. Any module that publishes must do `folder.children = publishedChildren; folder.sequenceNumber = newSequenceNumber; core.folderTree.set(...)`. Encode this as the only sanctioned write path; do not add a second publish helper.\n- **Preserve the guards verbatim:** the “existing.sequenceNumber >= result.sequenceNumber” checks and the post-await re-read in `adoptSharedFolderResult` must move as intact blocks (no behavioral edits during extraction). `client-load-reconcile.test.ts` is the regression net — it must pass unchanged at Phases 0, 3, 5, 6.\n- **`requireFolder` chokepoint stays singular:** keep one `requireFolder` on `core` so a newly-split Ops method cannot silently skip the self-heal/`ensureFolderLoaded` fallback (which is exactly the “Folder not loaded” + stale-ref failure class).\n\n### Stable public API\n- `index.ts` export list and every method signature are **frozen**. The facade re-exposes them identically; `BinNotLoadedError` stays exported from `client.ts`.\n- `@internal`-tagged accessors `getContext`, `getFolderTree`, `getConfig`, `emitEvent`, and `ensureFolderLoaded`, `registerFolder` are **in fact called by `apps/web`** (`folder-helpers.ts:27`, `useFileBrowserActions.ts:124`, `useFolderNavigation.ts:240`). Treat them as load-bearing public API — keep them on the facade, do not rename, do not remove the tag-implied behavior.\n- `ClientCore` and the new `ops/*` classes are **internal** — do NOT add them to `index.ts`. Adding exports would expand the public surface and is out of scope.\n- No `pnpm api:generate` needed (no `apps/api` change). Commit each phase on a `refactor/` branch via PR (never push to `main`).\n\n---\n\n## Relevant file paths\n- Target to split: `/Users/myankelev/Code/random/cipher-box/packages/sdk/src/client.ts`\n- Convention templates: `/Users/myankelev/Code/random/cipher-box/packages/sdk/src/bin/index.ts`, `/Users/myankelev/Code/random/cipher-box/packages/sdk/src/share/index.ts`, `/Users/myankelev/Code/random/cipher-box/packages/sdk/src/share/context.ts`\n- Public barrel (freeze): `/Users/myankelev/Code/random/cipher-box/packages/sdk/src/index.ts`\n- State containers: `/Users/myankelev/Code/random/cipher-box/packages/sdk/src/state/{folder-tree,shared-folder-tree,key-cache}.ts`\n- Guard tests: `/Users/myankelev/Code/random/cipher-box/packages/sdk/src/__tests__/`\n- External consumers proving `@internal` accessors are public: `/Users/myankelev/Code/random/cipher-box/apps/web/src/hooks/folder-helpers.ts:27`, `/Users/myankelev/Code/random/cipher-box/apps/web/src/components/file-browser/useFileBrowserActions.ts:124`, `/Users/myankelev/Code/random/cipher-box/apps/web/src/hooks/useFolderNavigation.ts:240`",
  "libDeepDive": "I have a complete picture. The desktop app constructs `CipherBoxFS` directly via struct literal (all fields must stay `pub`), uses the supporting types, `replay_for_vault`, `merge_folder_children`, `PublishCoordinator`, and the `platform`/`inode`/`cache`/etc. modules. Now I'll produce the plan.\n\n# Refactor Plan: Break up `crates/fuse/src/lib.rs` (3276 LoC)\n\n## 1. What `lib.rs` contains today (grouped by responsibility)\n\nReading the whole file, `lib.rs` is doing eight distinct jobs. Approximate line ranges:\n\n| # | Group | Lines | Items |\n|---|-------|-------|-------|\n| A | **Crate root**: module declarations, re-exports, doc comment | 1–36 | `pub mod` decls, `pub use` re-exports |\n| B | **Runtime/timeout shim** | 40–74 | feature-gated `use`s, `NETWORK_TIMEOUT`, `block_with_timeout` |\n| C | **Background-task message types** | 76–135 | `PendingRefresh`, `PendingContent`, `PendingFilePointer`, `FsEvent`, `UploadComplete` (enums + structs sent over the FS mpsc channels) |\n| D | **IPNS publish coordination + sequence math** | 185–343 | `PublishQueueEntry`, `next_file_publish_sequence`, `resolve_ipns_for_replay`, `classify_resolve_outcome`, `PublishCoordinator` (struct + impl) |\n| E | **Metadata encrypt/merge + background publish spawners** | 137–183, 345–888 | `spawn_metadata_refresh`, `encrypt_metadata_to_json`, `merge_folder_children`, `spawn_metadata_publish`, `spawn_bin_entry_publish`, `REENCRYPT_MAX_ATTEMPTS`, `ReencryptOutcome`, `resolve_and_fetch_file_meta`, `spawn_file_meta_reencrypt` |\n| F | **`CipherBoxFS` struct + inherent impl** | 890–1382 | struct def (B-group fields) and methods: `get_folder_key`, `build_folder_metadata`, `update_folder_metadata`, `drain_upload_completions`, `queue_publish`, `flush_publish_queue`, `drain_refresh_completions`, `drain_content_prefetches`, `drain_filepointer_completions` |\n| G | **Journal replay (crash recovery)** | 1384–2251 | `publish_file_metadata` re-export shim, `replay_for_vault`, `resolve_folder_key`, `resolve_folder_key_cached`, `fetch_merge_publish_parent`, `publish_child_folder_metadata`, `replay_mkdir_entry`, `replay_upload_entry` |\n| H | **Misc helpers + tests** | 2253–3276 | `uuid_from_ino`, `mount_point`, `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` (pure-fn + replay tests), `mod handler_harness_tests`, `mod durability_characterization_tests` |\n\nExisting crate conventions to follow (confirmed from `operations.rs`, `journal_helpers.rs`, `platform/mod.rs`):\n- Op modules wrap their body in `pub(crate) mod implementation { ... }` gated on `#[cfg(feature = \"fuse\")]`.\n- Cross-platform-shared, non-FUSE-callback code (like `journal_helpers.rs`) is gated on `#[cfg(any(feature = \"fuse\", feature = \"winfsp\"))]` at the *item* level, not wrapped in `implementation`.\n- Inherent `impl CipherBoxFS` blocks live in multiple files already (`journal_helpers.rs` adds methods to `CipherBoxFS`), so **splitting the impl across files is already an established pattern** — Rust allows multiple inherent `impl` blocks for one type across modules in the same crate.\n\n## 2. Public API constraint (must not break)\n\nExternal consumers (`apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/fuse/mod.rs`, `.../windows/mod.rs`) reference, by path `cipherbox_fuse::<X>`:\n\n- Modules: `cache`, `constants`, `file_handle`, `helpers`, `inode`, `platform`\n- Types: `CipherBoxFS` (**constructed via struct literal — every field must stay `pub`**), `PublishCoordinator`, `PendingRefresh`, `PendingContent`, `PendingFilePointer`, `UploadComplete`, `FsEvent`\n- Fns: `replay_for_vault`, `merge_folder_children`, (and `PublishCoordinator::new`)\n\n**Hard rule:** all of these must remain reachable at exactly `cipherbox_fuse::<same-name>`. The refactor moves *definitions* into new modules but `lib.rs` re-exports them with `pub use`, so every existing path resolves unchanged. `CipherBoxFS`'s fields stay `pub` (the desktop struct literal depends on it). The internal `use crate::operations::implementation::publish_file_metadata` shim and all `crate::error::IpnsResolveOutcome` paths stay valid because they're crate-relative.\n\n## 3. Target module tree\n\nNew files under `crates/fuse/src/` (siblings of the existing op modules):\n\n```\nsrc/\n  lib.rs                 # SHRINKS to ~120 LoC: module decls + re-exports + crate doc\n  runtime.rs        (B)  # NETWORK_TIMEOUT, block_with_timeout\n  events.rs         (C)  # PendingRefresh, PendingContent, PendingFilePointer, FsEvent, UploadComplete\n  publish.rs        (D)  # PublishQueueEntry, PublishCoordinator(+impl), next_file_publish_sequence,\n                         #   resolve_ipns_for_replay, classify_resolve_outcome\n  metadata.rs       (E)  # encrypt_metadata_to_json, merge_folder_children, spawn_metadata_refresh,\n                         #   spawn_metadata_publish, spawn_bin_entry_publish,\n                         #   spawn_file_meta_reencrypt (+ ReencryptOutcome, REENCRYPT_MAX_ATTEMPTS,\n                         #   resolve_and_fetch_file_meta)\n  fs.rs             (F)  # struct CipherBoxFS + impl CipherBoxFS (the 9 methods), uuid_from_ino, mount_point\n  replay.rs         (G)  # replay_for_vault + all replay helpers + publish_file_metadata shim use\n  (existing) cache.rs, constants.rs, error.rs, file_handle.rs, helpers.rs, inode.rs,\n             journal_helpers.rs, operations.rs, read_ops.rs, write_ops.rs, dir_ops.rs,\n             test_support.rs, platform/\n```\n\n### Item → module mapping\n\n- **`runtime.rs`**: `NETWORK_TIMEOUT`, `block_with_timeout`. (Note: `operations.rs::implementation` has its *own* separate `NETWORK_TIMEOUT`/`block_with_timeout` at 3s — leave that one alone; it's a distinct private copy.)\n- **`events.rs`**: the five message types (group C). No behavior, just `pub` data carriers. Make `pub`, keep `#[cfg(any(feature=\"fuse\", feature=\"winfsp\"))]`.\n- **`publish.rs`**: group D. `PublishCoordinator` and its impl move wholesale. `classify_resolve_outcome` is `fn` (pub(crate) — it's referenced by the test module via `super::classify_resolve_outcome`; see §5). `resolve_ipns_for_replay` is `async fn` used by `replay.rs` → make `pub(crate)`. `next_file_publish_sequence` is already `pub` and referenced by `operations.rs` as `crate::next_file_publish_sequence` → **re-export from lib.rs** to keep that path.\n- **`metadata.rs`**: group E. `merge_folder_children` and `encrypt_metadata_to_json` are `pub` (former is external API). `spawn_*` fns stay `pub` (`spawn_metadata_refresh`, `spawn_metadata_publish`, `spawn_bin_entry_publish`, `spawn_file_meta_reencrypt` are all `pub`). `ReencryptOutcome` + `REENCRYPT_MAX_ATTEMPTS` + `resolve_and_fetch_file_meta` are private → `pub(crate)`/module-private within `metadata.rs`.\n- **`fs.rs`**: group F + the two misc helpers from H (`uuid_from_ino`, `mount_point`). `build_folder_metadata` calls `uuid_from_ino`, so co-locate it here as a private `fn`. `mount_point` is `pub`. The struct keeps all `pub` fields. Methods stay `pub`/`pub(crate)` as today (`flush_publish_queue` is private → keep it module-private within `fs.rs`; it's only called by other `CipherBoxFS` methods in the same file, so no visibility change needed).\n- **`replay.rs`**: group G entirely. `replay_for_vault` is `pub` (external). All helpers (`resolve_folder_key`, `resolve_folder_key_cached`, `fetch_merge_publish_parent`, `publish_child_folder_metadata`, `replay_mkdir_entry`, `replay_upload_entry`) are private → keep module-private in `replay.rs`. The `use crate::operations::implementation::publish_file_metadata` (and winfsp variant) shim moves here verbatim since only replay uses it.\n\n### `lib.rs` after refactor (skeleton)\n\n```rust\n//! CipherBox FUSE filesystem implementation. (existing crate doc)\n\npub mod cache;\npub mod constants;\npub mod error;\npub mod file_handle;\npub mod helpers;\npub mod inode;\npub mod journal_helpers;\n\n#[cfg(any(feature = \"fuse\", feature = \"winfsp\"))] mod runtime;\n#[cfg(any(feature = \"fuse\", feature = \"winfsp\"))] mod events;\n#[cfg(any(feature = \"fuse\", feature = \"winfsp\"))] mod publish;\n#[cfg(any(feature = \"fuse\", feature = \"winfsp\"))] mod metadata;\n#[cfg(any(feature = \"fuse\", feature = \"winfsp\"))] mod fs;\n#[cfg(any(feature = \"fuse\", feature = \"winfsp\"))] mod replay;\n\n#[cfg(feature = \"fuse\")] pub mod dir_ops;\n#[cfg(feature = \"fuse\")] pub mod operations;\n#[cfg(feature = \"fuse\")] pub mod read_ops;\n#[cfg(feature = \"fuse\")] pub mod write_ops;\n\npub mod platform;\n\n#[cfg(all(test, feature = \"fuse\"))] mod test_support;\n\n// --- Stable re-exports (existing public surface) ---\npub use cache::{ContentCache, MetadataCache};\npub use error::FuseError;\npub use file_handle::OpenFileHandle;\npub use inode::{InodeData, InodeTable};\n\n#[cfg(any(feature = \"fuse\", feature = \"winfsp\"))]\npub use runtime::block_with_timeout;\n#[cfg(any(feature = \"fuse\", feature = \"winfsp\"))]\npub use events::{FsEvent, PendingContent, PendingFilePointer, PendingRefresh, UploadComplete};\n#[cfg(any(feature = \"fuse\", feature = \"winfsp\"))]\npub use publish::{next_file_publish_sequence, PublishCoordinator, PublishQueueEntry};\n#[cfg(any(feature = \"fuse\", feature = \"winfsp\"))]\npub use metadata::{\n    encrypt_metadata_to_json, merge_folder_children, spawn_bin_entry_publish,\n    spawn_file_meta_reencrypt, spawn_metadata_publish, spawn_metadata_refresh,\n};\n#[cfg(any(feature = \"fuse\", feature = \"winfsp\"))]\npub use fs::{mount_point, CipherBoxFS};\n#[cfg(any(feature = \"fuse\", feature = \"winfsp\"))]\npub use replay::replay_for_vault;\n```\n\nRe-exporting `next_file_publish_sequence` from the root keeps `crate::next_file_publish_sequence` (used in `operations.rs:160` and `platform/windows/operations.rs`) resolving. Re-exporting all the rest keeps `cipherbox_fuse::<X>` stable for the desktop app.\n\n## 4. Rust-specific concerns\n\n**Trait impl vs inherent impl.** The `impl Filesystem for CipherBoxFS` block already lives in `operations.rs` (not lib.rs) — untouched by this refactor. The inherent `impl CipherBoxFS { ... }` (group F) moves to `fs.rs`. Multiple inherent impl blocks across modules are legal (`journal_helpers.rs` already adds one), so no orphan-rule issue: `CipherBoxFS` and all its impls are defined in this crate. **The struct definition must be in scope wherever an impl block targets it** — `fs.rs` owns the `struct`, every other file (`journal_helpers.rs`, `operations.rs`) references it via `crate::CipherBoxFS` (re-exported) which keeps working.\n\n**Visibility changes needed (the only ones):**\n- `resolve_ipns_for_replay`, `classify_resolve_outcome` — currently file-private `fn`s in lib.rs, consumed by replay logic now in a *different* file → bump to `pub(crate)`.\n- `resolve_and_fetch_file_meta`, `ReencryptOutcome`, `REENCRYPT_MAX_ATTEMPTS` — only used inside `metadata.rs` → keep private (no change).\n- `uuid_from_ino`, `flush_publish_queue` — only used inside `fs.rs` → keep private.\n- Everything `pub` today stays `pub`. Everything else (`get_cached`, `update_cache` on `PublishCoordinator`) stays private within `publish.rs`.\n\n**`#[cfg(test)] mod tests` (group H).** The inline tests reference `super::next_file_publish_sequence`, `super::classify_resolve_outcome`, `super::merge_folder_children`, `super::PublishCoordinator`, `super::replay_for_vault`. After the move, `super::` from a `lib.rs`-level test module still resolves **because of the root re-exports** — except `classify_resolve_outcome`, which is `pub(crate)` not re-exported (it's internal). Two clean options:\n\n- **Option A (recommended):** move each pure-unit test next to its code. `next_file_publish_sequence_*` and `classify_resolve_outcome_*` → `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` inside `publish.rs`; `merge_folder_children_*` / `empty_name_merge_collision` / `not_found_outcome_drives_first_publish` → inside `metadata.rs` (or `publish.rs` for the outcome one); the replay `#[tokio::test]`s (`replay_for_vault_does_not_touch_failed_entries`, `legacy_empty_name_parks`, `strict_resolve_bypasses_cache`, `transient_failure_retains_entry`, `replay_records_failure_and_parks_at_max_retries`) → `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` inside `replay.rs` (they use `super::replay_for_vault`/`super::PublishCoordinator`). This keeps tests co-located with code and `super::` paths trivially correct.\n- **Option B:** keep one `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` in lib.rs and rewrite `super::X` → `crate::X`. Works for everything re-exported; needs `crate::publish::classify_resolve_outcome` for the one non-re-exported fn. More churn in the test bodies.\n\nGo with **Option A** — it minimizes edits inside test bodies and matches the \"co-locate\" intent of the existing module split.\n\n**The two harness test modules** (`handler_harness_tests`, `durability_characterization_tests`, lines 2946–3276) are gated `#[cfg(all(test, feature = \"fuse\"))]` and reference `crate::test_support`, `crate::read_ops`, `crate::write_ops`, `crate::FsEvent`, `crate::inode`, `crate::PublishCoordinator`. They exercise FUSE *handlers* across modules, so they don't belong to any single new module → **leave them in lib.rs** (or move to a dedicated `#[cfg(all(test, feature=\"fuse\"))] mod handler_tests;` file declared in lib.rs). All their `crate::` paths stay valid via the re-exports. Keeping them is the lowest-risk choice; this is where the bulk of the FUSE behavioral guard lives.\n\n**Platform split is unaffected.** `platform/` (macos/linux behind `fuse`, windows behind `winfsp`) and `platform/windows/operations.rs` (its own `publish_file_metadata`) are untouched. The conditional `use` shim in `replay.rs` keeps the same two `#[cfg]` arms verbatim.\n\n**Feature gating.** Apply the *same* gate the items currently carry. Groups B–G are all `#[cfg(any(feature = \"fuse\", feature = \"winfsp\"))]` today, so the new modules and their re-exports get that gate. Don't widen or narrow it.\n\n## 5. Phased extraction sequence (each phase compiles + passes tests independently)\n\nEach phase is one `cargo build` + `cargo test` gate. Run **both** feature sets at each phase — the crate is consumed by both fuser and WinFsp builds:\n\n```\ncargo test -p cipherbox-fuse                              # default (fuse)\ncargo build -p cipherbox-fuse --no-default-features --features winfsp\n```\n\n(The `winfsp` build is the one most likely to surface a missed `#[cfg]` gate, since most code is `any(fuse, winfsp)` but tests are `fuse`-only.)\n\n**Phase 0 — baseline.** Run the two commands above on the untouched tree; record green. This is the guard baseline. The FUSE behavioral tests (`handler_harness_tests`, `durability_characterization_tests`) and the replay tests are what protect the move — they construct a real `CipherBoxFS`, call handlers, and assert journal/inode/reply behavior, so any broken wiring (wrong field visibility, dropped re-export, mis-gated item) fails compilation or assertion.\n\n**Phase 1 — leaf modules with no internal deps: `runtime.rs`, `events.rs`.** Pure data + the timeout shim; depend on nothing in lib.rs. Move, add re-exports, build/test. Lowest risk — flushes out the re-export mechanics early.\n\n**Phase 2 — `publish.rs`.** Move group D. Set `resolve_ipns_for_replay`/`classify_resolve_outcome` to `pub(crate)`. Re-export `PublishCoordinator`, `PublishQueueEntry`, `next_file_publish_sequence`. Move the `next_file_publish_sequence_*` + `classify_resolve_outcome_*` unit tests into `publish.rs`. Verify `operations.rs`'s `crate::next_file_publish_sequence` and `crate::PublishCoordinator` still resolve.\n\n**Phase 3 — `metadata.rs`.** Move group E (depends on `publish::PublishCoordinator`, `merge_folder_children`, `encrypt_metadata_to_json`). Re-export the `spawn_*` + `encrypt_metadata_to_json` + `merge_folder_children`. Move the `merge_folder_children_*` / `empty_name_merge_collision` tests here.\n\n**Phase 4 — `fs.rs`.** Move the `CipherBoxFS` struct + inherent impl + `uuid_from_ino` + `mount_point`. This is the highest-blast-radius move (everything references `crate::CipherBoxFS`), so do it as its own phase. Keep all fields `pub`. Re-export `CipherBoxFS` and `mount_point`. After this, `journal_helpers.rs`, `operations.rs`, `test_support.rs`, and the desktop crate should all still compile unchanged (they use `crate::CipherBoxFS` / `cipherbox_fuse::CipherBoxFS`). The `durability_characterization_tests` (which build a `CipherBoxFS` and drive `handle_mkdir`/`handle_release`/`drain_upload_completions`) are the key guard for this phase.\n\n**Phase 5 — `replay.rs`.** Move group G last (it depends on `publish`, `metadata`, and the `operations::implementation::publish_file_metadata` shim). Move the replay `#[tokio::test]`s here. Re-export `replay_for_vault`. This phase proves the `#[cfg(feature=\"fuse\")]` vs `#[cfg(all(feature=\"winfsp\", not(feature=\"fuse\")))]` shim still picks the right `publish_file_metadata` — verify by running the `winfsp` build.\n\n**Phase 6 — clean lib.rs + final gate.** lib.rs now holds only module decls, re-exports, crate doc, and the two `#[cfg(all(test, feature=\"fuse\"))]` handler/durability test modules. Run the full crate test suite both feature sets, then `cargo build -p cipherbox-desktop` (or the desktop tauri crate) to confirm the downstream consumer compiles against the unchanged public surface. Optionally `cargo public-api diff` if available to assert zero public-API delta.\n\n### How the tests guard each phase\n- **Compilation is the first gate**: a dropped re-export breaks `operations.rs`/`journal_helpers.rs`/`test_support.rs`/desktop immediately.\n- **`#[cfg(all(test, feature=\"fuse\"))] handler_harness_tests + durability_characterization_tests`** construct a live `CipherBoxFS`, invoke real handlers, and assert journal-before-ack ordering and inode mutation — they catch any behavioral break in the `fs.rs` + channel-type moves (phases 1, 4).\n- **Replay `#[tokio::test]`s** (phase 5) assert journal park/retain/skip semantics through `replay_for_vault` — they catch a mis-wired `publish_file_metadata` shim or lost helper visibility.\n- **Pure-fn tests** (`next_file_publish_sequence`, `classify_resolve_outcome`, `merge_folder_children`) pin the sequence/merge contracts after they move (phases 2, 3).\n\nNo production behavior changes in any phase — every move is a cut-paste plus a re-export and (Option A) test relocation. Net result: `lib.rs` drops from ~3276 to ~120 LoC, with six new cohesive modules averaging ~150–600 LoC each, all matching the crate's existing `#[cfg]`-gated, `crate::`-referenced, multi-file-impl conventions.\n\n### Relevant file paths\n- Target: `/Users/myankelev/Code/random/cipher-box/crates/fuse/src/lib.rs`\n- Convention references: `/Users/myankelev/Code/random/cipher-box/crates/fuse/src/operations.rs`, `.../journal_helpers.rs`, `.../platform/mod.rs`, `.../test_support.rs`\n- Consumers to re-verify: `/Users/myankelev/Code/random/cipher-box/apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/fuse/mod.rs`, `.../fuse/windows/mod.rs`"
}

